# THE STOCK LOGIC — THE BOX'S CRONTAB, VERSIONED
# ==============================================
# This file IS the schedule. Nothing else in deploy/ carries cron lines any more:
# fundamentals.cron, learning.cron, market_flash.cron and meridian.cron were four
# separate fragments, which meant four places to look and no way to see a collision
# or a gap. They are folded in here and deleted.
#
# ██ INSTALL — MERGE. DO NOT RUN `crontab deploy/crontab.box`. ██
#
# THIS FILE CARRIES NO CREDENTIALS AND THE LIVE CRONTAB CARRIES NINETEEN.
# Installing this file on its own replaces the whole crontab, which deletes the
# environment-variable header every job depends on. Nothing would error: cron would
# run all 27 jobs with no keys, every Supabase write would 401, every broker login
# would fail, and the logs would fill with authentication errors that look like a
# provider outage. That is a worse failure than the schedule being unversioned,
# and an earlier revision of this header told you to do exactly it.
#
# The variable block is deliberately NOT committed -- it holds live tokens, and
# this repo is the thing that gets deployed to a public web host.
#
#     # 1. back up, always
#     crontab -l > ~/crontab.before.$(date +%F)
#
#     # 2. take the VARIABLE HEADER from the live crontab (every VAR=value line
#     #    above the first job), and the JOBS from this file
#     crontab -l | grep -E '^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=' > /tmp/ct.new
#     grep -vE '^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=' deploy/crontab.box >> /tmp/ct.new
#
#     # 3. READ IT before applying -- confirm the variable count and the job count
#     grep -cE '^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=' /tmp/ct.new    # expect 41
#     grep -cE '^[0-9*@]' /tmp/ct.new                    # expect 41
#     diff <(grep -E '^[0-9*@]' ~/crontab.before.*) <(grep -E '^[0-9*@]' /tmp/ct.new)
#
#     # 4. apply
#     crontab /tmp/ct.new
#
# Step 2 takes the header from the LIVE crontab rather than from a file, so a
# credential rotated on the box is never silently reverted to an older value.
#
# AND DO NOT APPEND EITHER. Appending doubles every job, and `rbe_engine` holds a
# websocket for the whole session -- two of those is two sets of detections written
# for every tick, into a table whose upsert key would not catch it.
#
# SHELL, PATH and MAILTO below are the only variables this file sets, because they
# are not secret and a wrong PATH is a failure mode of its own. If the live crontab
# also sets them, its values win in step 2 -- which is correct: the box knows its
# own paths.
#
# THE BOX RUNS UTC. IST = UTC + 5:30. Times are given in both because every
# decision here is about the Indian market session (09:15-15:30 IST).
#
# systemd, NOT cron, runs three things — atlas-market-hours.timer (the entry
# loop, currently DISABLED while ATLAS is paused), atlas-mis-squareoff.timer and
# atlas-engine-report.timer. Their units are in deploy/ and are installed
# separately with systemctl.
#
# ── WHAT CHANGED FROM WHAT THE BOX WAS RUNNING ON 2026-10-05 ─────────
#
#   REMOVED  atlas/signal/decay.py, every 10 minutes, 8 hours a day.
#            The file was deleted on 2026-10-02 as dead code. The cron line
#            survived it and has been failing 48 times a day into reports/atlas.log
#            ever since -- a missing-file error on a job nobody was reading the log
#            for. tests/test_crontab.py now fails if this file references a path
#            that does not exist.
#
#   MOVED    atlas/reporting/daily_report.py, 35 13 -> 45 13.
#            It shared a minute with update_outcomes.py and READS what that job
#            writes. Starting them together means the report is built from
#            whatever portion of the outcome update had landed, which is a
#            different number every night and never the right one.
#
#   ADDED    the four learning jobs. market_flash, reject_sample, excursions and
#            score_live_outcomes were written, tested, merged -- and never
#            installed. signal_excursions and reject_sample are empty because
#            nothing has ever run, not because they are waiting for tonight; the
#            page has shown "no market note" every session for the same reason.
#
#   LOGS     the four new jobs write to reports/, like the fifteen that came
#            before them, rather than /home/ubuntu/logs/. One place to look, and no
#            dependency on a directory outside the repo existing.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
MAILTO=""

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DEPLOY — every 5 minutes, all day, every day
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The only way code reaches the box. A commit on main is live within five
# minutes; nothing is pushed to the box by hand. `reset --hard` means an edit made
# ON the box is destroyed on the next tick, which is why no job may write to a
# tracked file.
*/5 * * * * cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && git fetch origin +refs/heads/main:refs/remotes/origin/main >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/git_sync.log 2>&1 && git reset --hard origin/main >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/git_sync.log 2>&1

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# BROKER SESSIONS — before the market opens
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Both tokens expire daily. Everything downstream reads them, so these run first
# and nothing else is scheduled before 08:25 IST.
#
# 02:55 UTC = 08:25 IST
55 2 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/zerodha_auto_login.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/atlas.log 2>&1
# 03:00 UTC = 08:30 IST — Upstox login and the Zerodha morning check share this
# minute deliberately: different brokers, no shared state, and both must be done
# before the 09:00 IST range-map build.
0 3 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/upstox_auto_login.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/login.log 2>&1
0 3 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 atlas/execution/zerodha_morning.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/atlas.log 2>&1

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THE INTRADAY TICKER — independent of ATLAS and of the pause
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 03:30 UTC = 09:00 IST. Builds data/processed/rbe/range_map.json for ~500 stocks
# before the open. rbe_engine refuses to start without a map stamped with today's
# IST date, so this must succeed first and 14 minutes is the margin.
30 3 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && ./venv/bin/python3 engine/rbe_startup.py >> reports/rbe.log 2>&1
# 03:44 UTC = 09:14 IST, one minute before the open. Holds a websocket for the
# whole session and exits 0 at close, which is why it is a daily cron start and
# not a service. Writes live_signals with kind='detection' -- observations, never
# calls, and never counted in the accuracy record.
44 3 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && ./venv/bin/python3 engine/rbe_engine.py >> reports/rbe.log 2>&1

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# INTRADAY REFRESHES
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Index quotes and the sector heatmap. 08:45 IST is pre-open on purpose: it seeds
# the previous close so the page is never blank at the open.
15 3 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/upstox_ws.py --update >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/live.log 2>&1
# 09:45 IST — the first half hour is settled
15 4 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/upstox_ws.py --update >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/live.log 2>&1
# 11:30 IST — midday
0 6 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/upstox_ws.py --update >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/live.log 2>&1
# 15:15 IST — the close, which is the figure the EOD chain and the page both quote
45 9 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/upstox_ws.py --update >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/live.log 2>&1

# 14:30 IST — buy-today-sell-tomorrow. The only intraday job that publishes CALLS
# rather than detections, which is why live_signals.kind exists.
0 9 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/btst_engine.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/btst.log 2>&1

# 15:45 IST — MERIDIAN's intraday IV snapshot. Runs at the close, deliberately
# before the 18:35 EOD comparison snapshot, and both are kept until the better
# time is settled by the data.
15 10 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m meridian.iv_recorder --label close >> /home/ubuntu/logs/meridian_iv_close.log 2>&1

# 15:35 IST — did yesterday's open ATLAS positions hit anything
5 10 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 atlas/execution/trade_outcome_checker.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/atlas.log 2>&1

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THE EOD CHAIN — 18:35 IST, one && chain, fail-closed
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CHAINED WITH &&, NOT SEPARATE JOBS, and that is the right call: 02b cannot score
# bars 01b did not download, and publishing a batch built on stale bars is worse
# than publishing none. A failure anywhere stops everything after it.
#
# THE COST OF THAT, STATED PLAINLY: a transient bhavcopy 500 at 18:35 means no
# signals that night, and the only notice is a line in reports/cron.log. The
# staleness check on signals.html is what catches it the next morning, which is
# twelve hours later than an alert would.
5 13 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/01b_download_bhavcopy.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/cron.log 2>&1 && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/build_market.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/cron.log 2>&1 && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/02b_smc_signals.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/cron.log 2>&1 && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/07_sector_momentum.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/cron.log 2>&1 && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/03b_score.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/cron.log 2>&1 && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/06_push_supabase.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/cron.log 2>&1 && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/mark_signals.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/cron.log 2>&1

# 18:35 IST — MERIDIAN's EOD snapshot, alongside the chain. Different API, no
# shared state, and the IV series cannot be back-filled so it does not wait.
5 13 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m meridian.iv_recorder --label eod >> /home/ubuntu/logs/meridian_iv_eod.log 2>&1

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# AFTER THE CHAIN — resolve, then measure, then report
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The order is a dependency chain even though the jobs are separate, so each has
# its own slot and the gaps are the margin.
#
# 19:05 IST — resolve yesterday's signals against today's bars
35 13 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/update_outcomes.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/cron.log 2>&1
# 18:50 IST — the desk note, from the figures the chain just published.
#
# NO `. /etc/atlas.env` HERE, and that is why this job produced no log file at all
# on its first night. /etc/atlas.env is root-owned and chmod 600; cron runs as
# ubuntu. The source failed with permission denied, the && chain short-circuited,
# python never ran, and the redirect never created the file -- a job that fails
# BEFORE its redirect leaves no trace at all, which is the worst way for a cron job
# to fail. The pattern was copied from the systemd units, which run as root and use
# EnvironmentFile.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY belongs in the crontab's own variable header alongside the other
# credentials. Without it market_flash takes its template path, which is permanent
# infrastructure rather than a fallback: the page always has a flash and it is never
# yesterday's prose.
# NO `set -a && . /etc/atlas.env && set +a &&` HERE, AND NEVER AGAIN. The
# installed line carried that prefix until 17 Oct 2026 and was dead the whole
# time: /etc/atlas.env is -rw------- root root, cron runs as ubuntu, the source
# failed with Permission denied, the && chain short-circuited and python never
# ran. Because the failure happened BEFORE the redirect, no log file was ever
# created -- reports/market_flash.log did not exist, and the market_flash table
# held zero rows. Syslog showed the job firing on 14, 15 and 16 Oct and leaving
# no trace of any kind. That is the worst way for a scheduled job to fail, and
# tests/test_crontab.py asserts "no job sources /etc/atlas.env" to keep it from
# coming back.
#
# The wrapper was pointless as well as fatal: all 8 variables in /etc/atlas.env
# are already crontab variables, and market_flash's own requirement is
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -- a crontab variable that is NOT in that file. Cron exports
# the variable block to every job; nothing needs to source anything.
20 13 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m engine.market_flash >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/market_flash.log 2>&1
# 19:00 IST — the negative class: 10 rejected stock-days per qualifying one, from
# all_rows_v2.parquet which 03b writes for the latest date only
30 13 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m engine.reject_sample >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/reject_sample.log 2>&1
# 19:10 IST — the 20-day forward path of every signal, detection and sampled
# reject not already measured. AFTER reject_sample, so tonight's sample is walked
# tonight.
40 13 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m engine.excursions >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/excursions.log 2>&1
# 19:15 IST — ATLAS's own daily report. MOVED off 35 13: it reads what
# update_outcomes writes and used to start in the same minute.
45 13 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 atlas/reporting/daily_report.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/atlas.log 2>&1
# 19:25 IST — the detection hypothesis, read off the paths written 15 minutes ago.
# Report only; writes nothing and is wired to no threshold.
55 13 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m engine.score_live_outcomes >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/detection_hypothesis.log 2>&1
# GSM/ASM SNAPSHOTS, THREE TIMES A SESSION: 10:30, 14:35 and 16:30 IST.
# NSE serves only the current list, so a session with no capture is gone for
# good and every observation window containing it scores surveillance_unknown.
# Three runs so one network failure cannot cost the day; the table's unique key
# makes the repeats a no-op. The close run SENDS A TELEGRAM ALARM naming the date
# if the session still has no ok capture.
0 5 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m engine.surveillance_snapshot --run morning >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/surveillance.log 2>&1
5 9 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m engine.surveillance_snapshot --run afternoon >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/surveillance.log 2>&1
0 11 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m engine.surveillance_snapshot --run close >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/surveillance.log 2>&1

# 19:35 IST — THE LEARNING LOOP. Extends every standing hypothesis by the
# observations that arrived since the last run, writes a ledger row either way, and
# reports ONLY when something crosses e-BH at alpha=0.05 across the whole standing
# set. Silence otherwise, deliberately: a nightly report nobody reads trains the
# operator to ignore the channel the real finding will arrive on.
#
# LAST, because it reads what everything before it wrote. Nothing reads it.
#
# It proposes; it never acts. The automatic gate needs a held-out period AND 200+
# live trades earned per finding, and ATLAS has 19 trades lifetime.
5 14 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m engine.learning_loop >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/learning.log 2>&1

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# FUNDAMENTALS — nightly refresh, weekly full fetch
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# fundamentals.gate() is consulted per candidate at decision time and reads ONLY
# the local cache, never the network: the market-hours loop cannot afford a
# request per symbol per cycle. data/processed is gitignored, so the deploy
# neither delivers this cache nor destroys it -- it has to be built here.
#
# 03:00 IST — announcements, every day
30 21 * * * cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m engine.tier1_fetch --all --announcements-only >> /home/ubuntu/logs/tier1_announcements.log 2>&1
# 04:10 IST — rebuild the gate cache from what was fetched
40 22 * * * cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m engine.fundamentals --refresh >> /home/ubuntu/logs/fundamentals_refresh.log 2>&1
# Saturday 01:30 IST — annual statements, which only change quarterly
0 20 * * 6 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m engine.fundamentals_fetch --all >> /home/ubuntu/logs/fundamentals_annual.log 2>&1
# Saturday 02:30 IST — the full tier-1 refetch
0 21 * * 6 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m engine.tier1_fetch --all --refetch >> /home/ubuntu/logs/tier1_full.log 2>&1

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THE TELEGRAM LISTENER
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# @reboot plus a 5-minute watchdog, because the listener is the only way an
# operator can halt or resume ATLAS from a phone and a dead listener is silent.
@reboot cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 atlas/reporting/bot_listener.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/bot.log 2>&1 &
*/5 * * * * /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/scripts/bot_watchdog.sh

# ── TSL FLASH — RADAR ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 19:20 IST — event detection, the extremes scanner, heat and the Hot 10.
# See docs/TSL_FLASH.md §13.
#
# ITS OWN ENTRY, NOT JOINED TO THE EOD CHAIN WITH &&, and that is the whole
# point of the placement. Radar CONSUMES the chain's bhavcopy and publishes
# nothing the screener depends on, so a crash here must cost Radar's night and
# nothing else. Joined with &&, a failure in this module -- the newest and least
# proven thing in the repo -- would take out signals publishing for the session.
# That failure has happened twice already (6125216, three sessions dark) from
# modules far better tested than this one.
#
# 15 MINUTES AFTER excursions (40 13) and 75 after the chain starts (05 13), so
# 01b_download_bhavcopy has long since written the parquets Radar reads. Radar
# does NOT download anything itself: if the session's bhavcopy is absent it
# refuses to score and exits non-zero rather than reporting a day of zeros.
#
# It carries the same completion check the chain has: it reads back what it
# wrote and exits non-zero plus Telegram when both the event and scanner counts
# come back zero. Either alone can legitimately be zero on a quiet session;
# both, across 706 symbols, means the write was rejected.
50 13 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m radar.run_detection >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/radar.log 2>&1

# ── ATLAS — THE PRE-CLOSE HANDOVER ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 15:20 IST (09:50 UTC). Day-0 SL orders become resting GTTs, and the trail runs.
# See docs/ATLAS_LONG_ONLY.md and atlas/execution/preclose_gtt.py.
#
# WHY THIS TIME AND NOT NEXT MORNING. A GTT checks the DEMAT account and shares
# bought today reach demat at T+1, so day 0 is protected by a regular SL order,
# which checks the ORDER BOOK. That SL has DAY validity and is flushed at 16:00
# ("all pending orders are cancelled at the end of the day"). If the GTT went in
# next morning the position would be naked overnight -- which is exactly when
# gaps happen. At 15:20 the SL is still live and a GTT cannot fire today, so the
# two overlap instead of leaving a window.
#
# ITS OWN ENTRY, NOT JOINED TO ANYTHING. A failure here means a position loses
# its stop at 16:00, so the job halts ATLAS and alerts rather than failing
# quietly -- and nothing else must be able to short-circuit it.
#
# THE TRAIL RUNS HERE TOO, once, after the close. No intraday churn: a stop that
# moves on every tick is a stop that gets hit by noise.
50 9 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m atlas.execution.preclose_gtt >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/atlas.log 2>&1

# ── ATLAS — THE SESSION REPORTS ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 11:30, 13:30, 15:30 IST and a day-end at 15:50, each CUMULATIVE SINCE 09:15.
# atlas/reporting/session_report.py. Reads only: no order is placed, modified or
# cancelled, so these run while halted and are most useful then.
#
# WHY SCHEDULED AND NOT PER CYCLE. The entry loop used to alert per blocked
# symbol per cycle -- 103 candidates failing one gate is 103 messages saying one
# thing -- plus the paused state re-alerted for as long as it persisted. The
# events (an entry, a self-halt, a protection failure, PRECLOSE BLIND) arrived in
# that same stream and were lost in it. The routine status now waits for these
# four; the events are untouched. atlas/reporting/cadence.py lists exactly what
# was silenced and why.
#
# THE 15:50 ONE IS 30 MINUTES AFTER preclose_gtt AND THAT IS THE POINT. It names,
# for every open long, which overnight GTT was placed and whether it CONFIRMED at
# the broker -- read back from get_gtts(), never from what ATLAS recorded
# attempting. If a position is open with no confirmed GTT that goes in the first
# line of the message. The exchange flushes day orders at 16:00, so 15:50 is the
# last moment a human can still fix it by hand.
#
# 06:00 UTC = 11:30 IST
0 6 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m atlas.reporting.session_report --slot 1130 >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/atlas.log 2>&1
# 08:00 UTC = 13:30 IST
0 8 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m atlas.reporting.session_report --slot 1330 >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/atlas.log 2>&1
# 10:00 UTC = 15:30 IST — the close
0 10 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m atlas.reporting.session_report --slot 1530 >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/atlas.log 2>&1
# 10:20 UTC = 15:50 IST — day-end, after the 15:20 GTT handover
20 10 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m atlas.reporting.session_report --slot dayend >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/atlas.log 2>&1

# ── THE PUBLIC HOME PAGE — ITS TWO FEEDS ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# Both are one-way producers: they read, and they write a table the browser can
# only SELECT. Neither can be invoked from the page.
#
# INDEX TILES. Nothing wrote NIFTY 50 / NIFTY BANK / NIFTY MIDCAP 100 /
# NIFTY SMLCAP 100 / INDIA VIX / USDINR before this; live_prices holds 745
# equities and not one index. Aligned to the live_prices refreshes so the strip
# and the heatmap are never from different moments. USDINR is resolved from the
# instrument master on every run, never pinned — it is a CDS future and it
# rolls; a pinned token goes stale on expiry and then dies.
#
# 03:15 UTC = 08:45 IST · 04:15 = 09:45 · 06:00 = 11:30 · 09:45 = 15:15
15 3 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/index_quotes.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/home_page.log 2>&1
15 4 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/index_quotes.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/home_page.log 2>&1
0 6 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/index_quotes.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/home_page.log 2>&1
45 9 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/index_quotes.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/home_page.log 2>&1
#
# THE TAPE. Opening-range breaks are the tape's primary content and they are
# genuinely minute-level, unlike the price feed. Published every 5 minutes
# across the session; the upsert key is (session_date, symbol) so re-publishing
# updates a break rather than repeating it.
#
# 03:00-10:55 UTC = 08:30-16:25 IST, which brackets the session at both ends.
*/5 3-10 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/publish_orb.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/home_page.log 2>&1
# THE LAST SESSION'S CLOSES, for the page's out-of-hours view. Runs after the
# nightly chain, which is what writes the parquet it reads. Without this the
# home page falls back to nothing after the close and renders a grey grid of a
# market that actually moved.
#
# 13:50 UTC = 19:20 IST, after the chain and before the nightly report.
50 13 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/publish_closes.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/home_page.log 2>&1
# WHAT THE BROKER ACTUALLY HOLDS against each open position, for the /atlas
# banner. That banner said "ATLAS does not place stop-losses" while every open
# position had a confirmed GTT resting; acting on it would have doubled up a
# stop. Read back from orders() and get_gtts(), never from exit_legs.
#
# Every 15 minutes across the session, plus once after the 15:20 handover so
# the overnight state is recorded.
#
# 03:00-10:55 UTC = 08:30-16:25 IST
*/15 3-10 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python3 engine/publish_protection.py >> /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/reports/home_page.log 2>&1
